data.content:
## Breaking Change in EF Core 11 (Cosmos Provider)

**Synchronous LINQ operations are no longer supported** on the Cosmos DB provider. The sync-over-async opt-in (`EnableSyncOverAsync`) that worked in EF Core 10 has been **removed**.

All four methods in your repository will throw `InvalidOperationException` at runtime:

| Method | Failing Call |
|---|---|
| `GetAll()` | `ToList()` |
| `GetById()` | `First()` |
| `GetCount()` | `Count()` |
| `Save()` | `SaveChanges()` |

## Fix: Convert to async

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

You'll need to propagate `async/await` up through all callers. The async LINQ methods are in `Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore` (already referenced).
